{"archetypes":[{"name":"exit-boundary","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The new hard/soft exit-1 distinction in design-log-publish.sh is a behavioral contract change; both SKILL.md callsites add `set +e` blocks that must parse PUBLISH_OK correctly, but the diff shows a likely syntax error (`${REPO:+--repo \"$REPO\"}\"` with a stray trailing quote before `2>`) in both Step 0b sub-step 3.3 and Step 5c item 9 that would cause a shell parse failure rather than capturing stdout.","prompt_body":"Examine every callsite in skills/design/SKILL.md (Step 0b sub-step 3.3 and Step 5c item 9) where design-log-publish.sh is invoked under `set +e`. Look specifically for shell syntax errors inside the command substitution — in particular, whether there is a stray `\"` character after `${REPO:+--repo \"$REPO\"}` and before the `2>` redirect. Verify that the `_publish_rc` / `_publish_out` capture pattern is syntactically valid and would actually suppress exit 1 before stdout is read. Also check whether any other callers of design-log-publish.sh in the diff (scripts/design-pause-save.sh references, any bash fences) are exposed to the new exit-1 paths without a matching `set +e` guard. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"staging-atomicity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Extracting the per-file staging logic into larch_log_publish_breadcrumbs_stage_file changes when `found_any=true` is set: the ndjson and quiet-log loops set it unconditionally after calling the helper, but the helper returns 0 for non-existent or non-regular files (early-return paths), meaning `found_any` can become true even though nothing was actually written to the staging dir, triggering an atomic swap of an empty breadcrumbs/ directory.","prompt_body":"In scripts/lib-larch-log.sh, trace the execution path in the refactored `larch_log_publish_breadcrumbs_shared` when a glob-matched file disappears between expansion and the helper's `-e`/`-f` checks: verify whether `found_any=true` is set and whether `larch_log_publish_breadcrumbs_swap` is subsequently called on an empty staging dir. Check the ndjson loop and the quiet-log loop separately. Also verify whether the `larch_log_publish_breadcrumbs_stage_file` helper's basename validation (`*/*|.*|*..*)` reject path) correctly removes `staging_parent` before returning 1 in all branches, or whether any early-return paths leave the staging dir orphaned. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"unplanned-export","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff adds `export DESIGN_TMPDIR` in design-log-publish.sh at line ~91, which does not appear in the implementation plan; exporting this variable into child processes (git, gh, redaction scripts) could cause larch_log_breadcrumbs_under_session_tmp to treat a foreign DESIGN_TMPDIR as an active session boundary in nested calls.","prompt_body":"In scripts/design-log-publish.sh, locate the newly added `export DESIGN_TMPDIR` line and determine why it was added — the plan does not mention it. Check whether any child process invoked by this script (git, gh, larch-log.sh, redact-tmpdir-paths.sh, redact-secrets.sh, or larch_log_publish_breadcrumbs_shared transitively) reads DESIGN_TMPDIR and could misinterpret it as an active session root, particularly via `larch_log_breadcrumbs_under_session_tmp`. Assess whether the export is necessary for the quiet-log staging path in the shared helper or whether it is an accidental side-effect. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
